# kanshi — automatic per-profile output config on hotplug/dock (Wayland replacement
# for the X11 monitor-setup xrandr logic). kanshi applies the profile whose set of
# outputs exactly matches what's connected. Positions are in LOGICAL pixels (after
# scale). Prefer INTEGER scales (fractional blurs apps without wp-fractional-scale-v1,
# e.g. Chrome) -- but on high-DPI panels (4K) a fractional scale's blur is minor and
# worth it for a usable size. Workspace->output assignment lives in wm/sway-only.

# Home: ultrawide (ASUS VG34VQL3A) left at native 1x, laptop to its right at 2x.
profile home {
    output HDMI-A-1 enable mode 3440x1440 scale 1 position 0,0
    output eDP-1 enable mode 3200x2000 scale 2 position 3440,0
}

# Office: Samsung 32" 4K (DP-3). INTEGER scale 1 so everything is crisp -- windowed
# Chrome blurs at fractional scales (Chromium's Wayland fractional support is still too
# raw as of 2026-09, even with --enable-features=WaylandFractionalScaleV1: sharp only in
# fullscreen). 1x is a bit small on 32" 4K -> use Chrome page-zoom (~110-125%) and bump
# app fonts as needed. Laptop at 2x to its right (3840 logical wide).
profile office {
    output DP-3 enable mode 3840x2160 scale 1 position 0,0
    output eDP-1 enable mode 3200x2000 scale 2 position 3840,0
}

# Laptop only. Slightly smaller than docked (2): you sit closer to the laptop when
# it's the only screen. 1.75 is fractional -> minor blur, but negligible at 236 DPI.
# Bump back to 2 if the blur bothers you.
profile laptop {
    output eDP-1 enable mode 3200x2000 scale 1.75 position 0,0
}
